.env
service-account.json
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/
logs/*.log
.DS_Store
# NOTE: data/run_state.json is intentionally NOT ignored — the GitHub
# Actions workflow commits it back to the repo after every run so resume
# state survives between runs (each run starts on a fresh VM with no
# local disk continuity, so if this were ignored, resume would never
# actually work across separate workflow executions).
#
# Feature 3 (Smart Alert System): data/alert_state.json follows the exact
# same pattern and is also intentionally NOT ignored — it's what makes
# alert deduplication/recovery detection work across separate workflow
# runs (see notification_manager.py).
#
# Feature 4 (Intelligent Monitoring Scheduler): data/page_schedule_state.json
# follows the same pattern too — it's what lets the scheduler know each
# page's last successful run across separate hourly workflow executions.

# Feature 2 (Customer Journey Monitoring): failure/success screenshots are
# written here during a run, then uploaded as a GitHub Actions artifact by
# monitor.yml — deliberately never committed to the repo (would bloat repo
# size fast at hourly cadence).
journey_screenshots/
